  // WI-M3-03 cross-game points budget and the two asymmetric 1000-unit roster manifests.
  // Rates (authored): Generals BuildCost converts 1:1 to points; EE2 unit resource columns
  // (db/TechTree/upgrade_unittypes.csv, summed) convert at 5 points per resource unit, the
  // median of the counterpart anchors (Crusader 900 vs 159, BattleMaster 800 vs 159, Raptor
  // 1400 vs 280, Aurora 2500 vs 500, Comanche 1500 vs 145, Tomahawk 1200 vs 400). Generals
  // infantry are premium (Ranger 225 vs 119 resources); recorded as an accepted deviation
  // rather than a per-class rate. Tolerance 0.5 percent of the larger total.
  // Both sides carry anti-air (marked entries) and aircraft; aircraft count toward the 1000
  // and airfields do not (they are not units). Compositions differ deliberately: a
  // Generals-led armor-heavy army against an EE2-led mass army, each with Generals AA mixed in.
  "Name": "mass-battle-rosters",
